Link ccv and NNC as one shared library

Six binaries each carry a private copy of the ~970 MB .nv_fatbin plus all ccv
host code and sqlite. WORKSPACE.linux pre-declares @sqlite3 with a split BUILD
and hands @s4nnc two patches, which add a cc_shared_library and a cc_import to
nnc/BUILD.bazel and pass @ccv its own patch marking the host sub-libraries
alwayslink. The four cuda_library targets stay lazy, because their members
ride the registrant references in the committed ccv_nnc_cmd.inc and forcing
them would embed kernels the binaries never carried. Eight Libraries BUILD
files redirect @ccv//lib:ccv to @s4nnc//nnc:C_ccv so the static payload cannot
leak back in. One sqlite copy lives in the shared library, because Store.swift
opens handles that ccv_nnc_tensor_read consumes.
